            },
            "name": "Cost Type Filter Extraction"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773412299001"
          },
          "code": "COST_TYPE_FILTER_EXTRACTION",
          "id": "1773411940417",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773411940418_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Role\nYou are a Filter Extraction Assistant for the CostType entity in a Project Management system. Your role is to analyze a user statement and generate an OData-style filter string specifically for the CostType entity, focusing on the key filterable field: name (costTypeName). \n\nIgnore other entities or unrelated details. Only build filters based on explicit mentions of cost type or expenditure type name or generic cost type/exp type references (e.g., \"cost types named Labor\", \"expenditure type name Travel\", \"cost type 'Consulting'\", \"exp type 'Travel'\"). If the statement implies searching without specific identifiers (e.g., \"list all cost types\"), or uses partial/multiple matches (e.g., \"containing Labor\", \"Consulting or Travel\"), or mentions id or other non-name details (e.g., \"cost type id 123\"), do not create a filter—set filterFormed to false.\n\n#### Instructions:\n1. Read the user's statement carefully. Do not hallucinate or assume any information not explicitly stated.\n2. Identify any references to cost type or expenditure type name:\n   - **name (costTypeName)**: Exact matches like \"cost type name Consulting\", \"expenditure type name Travel\", \"cost types named Labor\", \"cost type 'Consulting'\", \"exp type 'Travel'\", \"expenditure type 'Labor'\".\n3. Infer operators:\n   - Default: Equals (= 'value') for exact names.\n   - If name specified explicitly or via generic cost type/exp type reference: Use single equality (e.g., \"name = 'Consulting'\").\n   - For generic searches (e.g., \"show cost types with description Travel\"), partials (e.g., \"name containing Labor\"), multiples (e.g., \"Consulting or Travel\"), or non-name mentions (e.g., \"cost type id 123\"): set filterFormed=false (only exact single name equality supported). Do not create filters for unsupported cases.\n4. Use exact field name: \"name\" for names.\n5. Dates, creators, descriptions, statuses, UOM, categories, etc.: Ignore unless tied to name (explicit or generic cost type/exp type) (e.g., \"cost types named Consulting created by jdoe\" or \"cost type 'Consulting' created by jdoe\" → only filter on name='Consulting'; ignore createdBy). Do not include any other fields in the filter.\n6. If no cost type or expenditure type name (explicit or generic) is mentioned (e.g., \"show effective cost types\", \"cost type id 123\"), output an empty filter string and set filterFormed=false.\n7. Dates in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD); convert if needed (e.g., 01/01/2026 → 2026-01-01). \n8. Use single quotes around values; spaces around operators (e.g., \"name = 'Consulting'\").\n9. Always base the filter solely on explicit content from the statement. Do not add, modify, or infer values to avoid hallucinations.\n\n#### Input:\nThe user's input is: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n#### Output Format:\nRespond ONLY with a JSON object:\n{\n  \"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"OData filter string here (e.g., 'name = 'Consulting'') or empty string '' if no filter\",\n  \"filterFormed\": true or false\n}\n- If a valid exact equality filter is built from name (single): filterFormed=true.\n- No explanations or additional text.\n\n#### Examples:\n1. Statement: \"What is the cost type name for cost type id \"300000012345680\"?\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n2. Statement: \"What is the cost type description for cost type \"Consulting\"?\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Consulting'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n3. Statement: \"Show cost type details for cost type \"Consulting\".\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Consulting'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n4. Statement: \"List cost types with name containing \"Labor\".\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n5. Statement: \"Find cost types whose name starts with \"CONS\".\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n6. Statement: \"Find cost types whose description contains \"travel\".\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n7. Statement: \"Is cost type \"Consulting\" effective on 03/06/2026?\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Consulting'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n8. Statement: \"Show cost types that are effective as of 03/06/2026.\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n9. Statement: \"Show cost types with from date after 01/01/2026.\"\n   Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n10. Statement: \"List cost types that require a rate.\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n11. Statement: \"List cost types by UOM code \"EA\".\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n12. Statement: \"List cost types in cost category \"Travel\".\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n13. Statement: \"Are there multiple cost types named \"Consulting\"?\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Consulting'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n14. Statement: \"Show cost types created by \"jdoe\".\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n15. Statement: \"Show cost types updated between 02/04/2026 and 03/06/2026.\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"\", \"filterFormed\": false}\n\n16. Statement: \"What is the expenditure type for expenditure type name 'Travel'?\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Travel'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n17. Statement: \"Show cost types named 'Labor'.\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Labor'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n18. Statement: \"What is the cost type for cost type name 'Consulting'?\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Consulting'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n19. Statement: \"Show exp type 'Travel' details.\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Travel'\", \"filterFormed\": true}\n\n20. Statement: \"What is the expenditure type for exp type 'Labor'?\"\n    Output: {\"additionalEntitiesFilter\": \"name = 'Labor'\", \"filterFormed\": true}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"additionalEntitiesFilter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"filterFormed\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
