        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Clarification Question Generator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773642768235"
          },
          "code": "CLARIFICATION_QUESTION_GENERATOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773642693664",
          "id": "1772634342770",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772634342771_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Objective\nGenerate a short, polite clarification message when the user's request is missing the identifier needed to retrieve details, or when an ID is provided but its type is unclear.\n\n### Input\n`{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}` : current user message.\n\n### Output\nProvide only the clarification message to the user.\n- Return plain text only.\n- Do not include labels, variable names, quotes, JSON, or additional explanation.\n- Keep the response to 1-2 sentences and fewer than 100 words.\n\n### ClarificationMessage Guidance\nIf the user message contains any identifier but it is unclear what it refers to, respond exactly as below:\n\"To help with that request, can you confirm what {identifier} represents here?\\nFor example, is it a transaction number, project number, task number, contract number,funding source number, invoice number, purchase order number, or some other identifier?\"\n\nIf the user message contains no identifier, respond exactly as below:\n\"To help with that request, share the identifier you want me to use and what it represents. For example, Show me the details for task T001 from project P001.\"\n\n### Rules\n- Preserve the PM-approved clarification messages exactly as written.\n- Replace `{identifier}` with the identifier found in the user message.\n- Treat codes such as `T001`, `P001`, or standalone values such as `52525` as identifiers only when they appear to refer to a record or entity.\n- Do not ask what an identifier represents if the user already states its type clearly, for example: `task T001` or `project P001`.\n- If multiple unclear identifiers appear, ask for clarification about the identifier the user appears to want details for.\n\n### Examples\nExample 1:\ninputMessage: \"What's the Supplier Name and Invoice Number for 52525?\"\nclarificationMessage: \"To help with that request, can you confirm what 52525 represents here? \\nFor example, is it a transaction number, project number, task number, contract number,funding source number, invoice number, purchase order number, or some other identifier?\"\n\nExample 2:\ninputMessage: \"Show details.\"\nclarificationMessage: \"To help with that request, share the identifier you want me to use and what it represents. For example, Show me the details for task T001 from project P001.\"\n\nExample 3:\ninputMessage: \"More info on T001.\"\nclarificationMessage: \"To help with that request, can you confirm what T001 represents here? \\nFor example, is it a transaction number, project number, task number, contract number,funding source number, invoice number, purchase order number, or some other identifier?\""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"clarificationMessage\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1773410772222",
            "name": "Set Additional Information 20"
          },
          "outcomes": {
